      <dt>Resort type</dt><dd>Deluxe Villa resort at Disney's Beach Club Resort, in the EPCOT Resort Area. Disney Vacation Club inventory is mixed with cash bookings.</dd>
      <dt>Address</dt><dd>1800 Epcot Resorts Boulevard, Lake Buena Vista, FL 32830 (same campus as Beach Club; confirm check-in location on your reservation)</dd>
      <dt>Size</dt><dd>Villas attached to Beach Club, sharing Stormalong Bay, the walk to EPCOT's International Gateway, and the Friendship boat dock with Beach Club and Yacht Club.</dd>
      <dt>Rooms</dt><dd>Deluxe Studios sleep 5; one-bedroom villas sleep 4; two-bedroom villas sleep 8. A single child under 3 in a crib does not count toward the maximum. There is no Grand Villa category in the 2026 cash-rate table we used.</dd>
      <dt>Beds</dt><dd>Studio: 1 queen, 1 queen-size pull-down and 1 single pull-down. One-bedroom: 1 king and 1 queen-size pull-down. Two-bedroom: 1 king, 2 queens and 1 queen-size sleeper sofa or pull-down.</dd>
      <dt>Getting around</dt><dd>Walking paths and Friendship boats to EPCOT and Hollywood Studios. The EPCOT Skyliner station is a walk through the International Gateway. Buses to Magic Kingdom, Animal Kingdom, the water parks and Disney Springs</dd>
      <dt>Food</dt><dd>Shared with Beach Club and Yacht Club, including Cape May Cafe and Beaches &amp; Cream Soda Shop. See those hotel guides for the hours we last checked.</dd>
      <dt>Pools</dt><dd>Stormalong Bay, plus leisure pools that include one at Beach Club Villas. Official Beach Club pages describe three leisure pools in all, and say Yacht Club guests may use the villas pool as well.</dd>
