  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who Beach Club Villas are best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Families who want a kitchen and a fifth bed in a studio,</strong> within a short walk or boat of EPCOT and Hollywood Studios.</li>
      <li><strong>People who will actually use Stormalong Bay,</strong> and who may also want the quieter villas leisure pool.</li>
      <li><strong>Groups of eight who can use a two-bedroom villa</strong> instead of two hotel rooms.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You need a fifth bed in a one-bedroom.</strong> Official listings cap the one-bedroom at four adults.</li>
      <li><strong>Your parks are mostly Magic Kingdom or Animal Kingdom.</strong> Those are buses.</li>
      <li><strong>You are sensitive to exterior work.</strong> Official pages say Beach Club will have visible exterior maintenance through late 2027, which may affect some views and, at times, require alternate paths during the day.</li>
    </ul>
    <span class="ryan">[Ryan: who you think this resort is really for, from your own stays. Two or three sentences.]</span>
  </section>

  <section id="rooms">
    <h2>Room types, sizes and beds</h2>
    <p>This guide covers Beach Club Villas. The hotel rooms at <a href="/resorts/beach-club-resort/">Beach Club</a> and <a href="/resorts/yacht-club-resort/">Yacht Club</a> have their own pages. Guests share Stormalong Bay, the walk to EPCOT, the Friendship boats and the restaurants. Studios typically have a kitchenette; one-bedroom villas and larger typically have a full kitchen <span class="verify">[verify current appliances]</span>. There is no extra-adult charge up to the occupancy limit.</p>
